  m_Name: TerraTest
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::EventSequence
  events:
  - isDialogue: 1
    durationSeconds: 125
    unityEvent:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
    subtitles:
      text:
      - Hello there and welcome to my Terra test project.
      - So I've worked one a few things this week.
      - The two main ones are
      - the subtitles and the receipt system
      - there's also a kitchen manager
      - which you can't see and is not currently implemented
      - but I did program most of it.
      - so I'll start with the subtitles
      - you can see them now on the bottom of the screen
      - and if you continue forwards
      - there's a little counter
      - and a receipt has printed out of the
      - receipt printer at this point
      - you can interact with it
      - and if you do it'll show you an order
      - that's everything I was able to implement this week.
      - Unfortunately I didn't have as much time as I wanted.
      - However, there's a bunch of stuff I implemented before this.
      - We have the pathfinding system
      - which if you look underneath you
      - you can see the monster moving around
      - the IK system that that monster is using to move around
      - 'and I also programmed a '
      - Burger, like eating thing
      - Er, um not eating thing coo- building thing
      - '*uninteligable*'
      - you can follow the instructions on the receipt
      - to make an order
      - using the food elements behind you
      - I also programmed the inventory system
      - and if you press TAB you can open your inventory
      - you only have two slots
      - you can also scroll to choose which item is in your main slot
      - then if you place items (on a plate) on the counter
      - next to the receipt printer they will be served
      - and the number will tell you how many points you got
      - I plan on adding a lot more interactability this week
      - Including a
      - Including a bunch of animations which my friend is working on
      - oh that's another thing
      - all  the models here are made by my friend
      - then
      - so I plan on
      - implementing a bunch of animations
      - some sounds and more cooking stuff
      - That's about it thanks for checking it out
